      "text": [
        "796 - وَقَالَ زُرَارَةُ قَالَ أَبُو جَعْفَرٍ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ: «إِيَّاكَ وَ اِلْتِحَافَ اَلصَّمَّاءِ» قَالَ قُلْتُ وَ مَا اَلصَّمَّاءُ قَالَ «أَنْ تُدْخِلَ اَلثَّوْبَ مِنْ تَحْتِ جَنَاحِكَ فَتَجْعَلَهُ عَلَى مَنْكِبٍ وَاحِدٍ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.796 – Zurarah narrated that Abu Ja'far, Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir (as) said:\n\"Beware of the 'wrapped shroud' (al-samma').\"\nI asked: \"And what is the 'wrapped shroud'?\"\nImam (as) said: \"It is when you take your garment under your arm and place it over one shoulder”."
        ]
      }
    },
